WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.439 --> 00:00:02.800
Hey guys, Pete here.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.500
Today I'm going to do a Dark video to follow
up my family trees video from last year.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.890
At the end of that video I mentioned how many
unanswered questions we have about the family

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.070
connections in Netflix's Dark.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.010
This video will look at those with some of
the popular theories that surround them.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.420
I'm going to talk about everything we know
with plenty of speculation, so this will contain

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.160
spoilers if you haven't made it through the
first two seasons of Dark.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.780
This would be your chance to leave if you
wandered in here by mistake.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.850
The day after I made my video about the families
the team behind Dark released this official

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:35.850
family tree.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.440
Thiers looks great, but it didn't really add
any extra information to the dozens of fan

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.850
made ones that were already out there on the
internet.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.969
Beyond the arrangements of the characters
what was really interesting about this one

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:50.190
was the question marks they added in some
of the places.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.879
They really draw your attention to some of
the people we don't know.

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:58.050
I'm going to go around the family tree and
talk about each of those question marks, some

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:02.929
of the underlying mysteries, and the theories
people have about these complicated family

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.929
connections.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:08.890
We're obviously moving into new territory
in season 3, so this will only be discussing

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.550
the families in the Winden we spent the first
two seasons of Dark getting to know.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.580
We can start at the bottom, and the first
big question is who is Regina's father?

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.010
Claudia is a central figure in the story in
her role at the power plant, her time as a

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:27.920
traveller, and she earns the moniker of the
White Devil because of her influence in her

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.100
old age.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.420
The fact that they haven't revealed her the
father of her child seems intentional at this

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.660
point, and out of all different questions
the popular theory for this one is pretty

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.660
solid.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:43.020
Most fans would agree that Tronte Nielsen
is the best candidate because we know they

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.020
had a relationship.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:49.050
They knew each other as kids, and it's hinted
that they had an affair as adults based on

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.000
their interaction at the power plant.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.890
His wife was actually ready to leave him before
Mads disappeared because she knew he was cheating.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:01.340
There's several questions surrounding Tronte
as a character and we'll get into that later.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.690
But, here's what we know for him for sure
- he's married to his wife Jana, and the father

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.090
of Mads who went missing in the 1980s timeline.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:14.560
His other son is Ulrich Nielsen who is the
father of Magnus, Martha, and Mikkel in the

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.450
2019 timeline.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.500
So if Tronte is Regina's father that would
connect the Nielsen and Tiedemann families.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.320
Mikkel Nielsen travelled through time and
was taken in by Ines Kahnwald.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.780
That connects the Nielsens and the Kahnwalds,
and more importantly Jonas to Martha.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:33.370
Since Martha and Mikkel were siblings that
makes her Jonas's aunt.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:36.090
The next question mark is in the Kahnwald
family.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.890
Who is Daniel's wife and why is she important?

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:43.780
We've had mention of her in his conversations
with Egon at work, and we know their daughter.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.380
I think in this case it's hard to come up
with theories since we don't know why or even

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.570
if she's important to the big picture.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.350
It's notable that they haven't revealed her
identity, and that they made the choice to

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.459
add a question mark here on this family tree.

00:02:57.459 --> 00:03:02.510
After all we don't know who Hannah's mother
is, but her father Sebastian Kruger doesn't

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.740
have a question mark where his wife's name
would be.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.740
One female character that might be a candidate
is Silja.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:13.319
She fits in somewhere, and there's a possibility
that she might have a child in season 3 - which

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:17.790
I talked about in my the End is the Beginning
video, but there isn't enough groundwork to

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.840
turn this into a solid theory.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.860
Silja is a mysterious character.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:27.160
We know she is Elisabeth's sign language interpreter
in the 2050s timeline, and we know from this

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:34.120
blurb on the darknetflix2053 Instagram account
that Elisabeth is also her foster mother.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.060
Her image appears on Adam's big photo wall
below the main families off to the side of

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.540
Noah and Agnes.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:44.990
That hints that there might be more to learn
about her but doesn't tell us much else.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.160
The other place she might fit in is in the
Doppler family line.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.910
We don't know who Peter's mother is yet.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:55.060
In this case most of the theories revolve
around where Peter came from since he arrived

00:03:55.060 --> 00:04:00.780
in Winden in 1987, and if Helge is actually
his father in the first place.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.190
Based on his diminished state some fans have
questioned if he would have been able to father

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.190
a child.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:08.180
The simple answer is of course he could.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.800
Helge wasn't a bright kid, his mother was
cold and possibly cruel, and he certainly

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.489
experienced trauma at the hands of Ulrich
as a child.

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:20.030
None of the really translates to him being
unable to have a relationship though, and

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.720
we don't know what he was like as a young
man in the 33 year gap.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.240
He was manipulated into doing terrible things
by Noah, and it's possible that that wasn't

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.130
his only interaction with travellers.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:37.300
Peter's strange backstory of coming to come
to town in 1987 without any other details

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.190
has led some fans to speculate that he's a
time traveller himself.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:46.250
It's certainly possible, and the fact that
his teenage photo on Adam's wall is in black

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.020
and white makes you wonder.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:53.150
The thing that contradicts this is that he
seemed unaware of time travel before he witnessed

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.210
Mad's dead body arriving at the bunker.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:59.560
You could say that maybe he travelled as a
child like his wife Charlotte, so he didn't

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:05.090
have a memory of it, but then what is the
point of having him arrive in 1987.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.780
Before we move on to the biggest question
I have it's worth pointing out that Greta

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:13.240
Doppler hinted that Helge might not be Bernd's
biological son.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:19.130
As far as we can tell he raised him as he
was, but Greta told Noah that he was not conceived

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.130
by love.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.840
The theory is that she may have been raped,
but there isn't any evidence pointing to a

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.600
prime suspect.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.699
That leads us to the last question mark, and
arguably the biggest question of all - who

00:05:29.699 --> 00:05:32.060
is the father of Tronte Nielsen?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:36.460
His mother Agnes is also a mystery, and we
don't know who her parents are either.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.710
She's Noah sister.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:43.800
We saw her as a child in the 1920s timeline,
and she returned to Winden in the 1950s timeline

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.430
renting a room with Egon and Doris Tiedemann.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:50.540
There's been a lot of speculation about who
Noah and Agnes's parents were.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:54.200
One of the most popular theories is that it's
Magnus and Franziska.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:59.050
We know they do travel to the past, we know
they're part of Sic Mundus in the early days,

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:03.310
putting them in the right place, but it seems
odd when we meet Noah and Agnes that they're

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:08.010
being raised by Erna rather than their parents
who are in that same time.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:12.300
If this was the case the Nielsen family would
be a loop like the Doppler's.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.120
which it would be connected to through Franziska.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.070
We Agnes and Tronte arrive she described her
husband to Doris as a pastor that wasn't a

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.250
good man.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.500
Tronte had mysterious burns on his arm that
were never explained.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.090
They look like cigar burns.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:30.330
And, could be signs of self-harm, or signs
of an abusive father.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.050
As far as who that father is?

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.950
The most popular theory has been that it is
Bartosz.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:39.700
This is primarily because he is an important
character that we imagine would pair up with

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:40.700
someone.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:44.360
In my mind he doesn't seem like someone who
would burn their child, but as mentioned we

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.680
don't really know what's going on with the
injuries.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:51.320
They do factor into the most recent theory,
which is that the new character who appears

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.810
as a trio in the new trailers could be Tronte's
father.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.430
In the little bit of footage we've seen we
see the characters come off as menacing, and

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.690
they may be capable of harming children.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.820
At the same time we don't know much about
them, so it's really just a guess at this

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:05.820
point.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.960
Either way this new version of the family
tree that showed up in the trailer brings

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:13.500
up a lot of questions because it's mirrored
in the middle and joined with an infinity

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.500
sign.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.410
Agness is the character who is connected to
that sign with her son branching off from

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.410
there.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:24.920
This has led people to think perhaps whoever
is Agnes's mate is maybe involved with whatever

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.270
happened to cause these two worlds to split
off in the first place.

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:33.460
Another thing about this family tree that
I won't go into too deeply is the character

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:38.389
Boris Niewald who takes on the identity of
Aleksander Kohler, and then marries Regina

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:42.840
and becomes Aleksander Tiedemann who later
is running the power plant.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.630
Boris just shows up in the woods, and you
could really make a whole video about this

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.440
so I don't want to go too far.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.840
One of the things I know will get posted in
the comments if I don't bring it up though

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.270
is that his last name is Niewald.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:59.130
Which, if you put the name Nielsen and Kahnwald
together you get Niewald.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.440
This is a curious thing that they decided
to do.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:06.569
There's definitely more to this character
than we have to learn, but I really don't

00:08:06.569 --> 00:08:08.530
even have a favorite theory here.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:13.340
I think it's safe to say that Boris was manipulated
by time travellers.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:18.710
He's carrying the gun that will eventually
be used by Adam to kill Martha.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.590
So he has a connection there.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:25.889
Whether he was a traveller himself or he was
just put on his path by somebody who was working

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:30.330
behind the scenes for either Adam or Claudia
remains unclear.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:36.070
But fans really enjoy this idea that his last
name is Niewald and some speculate that perhaps

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:41.640
even though Hannah is in her late forties
when she travels back in time might have a

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:47.590
child and may give them this name as a combination
between Ulrich's last name and hers.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.170
Beyond that there is just one more thing I
want to mention and then I will wrap it up.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.149
On Adam's board there's one character who
is never been identified.

00:08:55.149 --> 00:08:58.360
I can't even really tell if it's a female
or a male.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.450
It looks like a young girl to me, but I've
seen a lot of people refer to it as a boy

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.589
and you really can't tell.

00:09:04.589 --> 00:09:05.910
It's above the families.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:11.250
It's to the side of where the missing children
are, and I'm really curious as to who this

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.250
is.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:16.640
So let me know if you have any theories about
this because it's strange that there's just

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:20.950
one picture on this entire thing that we can't
really agree on.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.870
So, with that I will end it here.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:28.160
I hope this clears up any additional questions
you had about the family tree.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.080
If not, please ask them in the comments.

